IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ohs-dates`
IMPORT `ohs-core`
IMPORT `ohs-seat`

-- Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004 (Vic) -- cases for the seat of the person at work: unsafe work (ss 74, 75),
-- discrimination for raising health and safety (ss 76-78E) and making WorkSafe prosecute (ss 131, 132). Every expected
-- value was worked by hand from the deposited text (Version No. 045), with the section and the arithmetic in the
-- comment; none was copied from the encoding's output.
--
-- Readings used (ohs-dates.l4): "within 3 months after", "within 6 months of", "within 2 years after" and "not more
-- than 1 year after" a day end on the same day of the later month, or the last day of a shorter month.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

GIVEN `dd` IS A NUMBER
      `mm` IS A NUMBER
      `yy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`d` `dd` `mm` `yy` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY `dd` `mm` `yy`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is the same day as` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` EQUALS DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `m` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `m` `is just the day` `b` IF
    CONSIDER `m`
    WHEN JUST `a` THEN `a` `is the same day as` `b`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN `m` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is no day` `m` IF
    CONSIDER `m`
    WHEN JUST `a` THEN FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- s 74. Inputs: issue, immediate threat, s 73 not appropriate, consulted, who directs.
#ASSERT `Can the work be stopped` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `the health and safety representative for the designated work group` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the work be stopped` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `the employer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the work be stopped` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `someone else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the work be stopped` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `the health and safety representative for the designated work group` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the work be stopped` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `the employer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the work be stopped` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `the employer` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 75(1). Inputs: a party, not resolved in a reasonable time, cease-work direction.
#ASSERT `Can I ask for an inspector` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I ask for an inspector` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I ask for an inspector` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I ask for an inspector` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 75(4). Inputs: did not work, otherwise paid, prohibition notice, written determination.
#ASSERT `Am I still paid for the time I did not work` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I still paid for the time I did not work` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I still paid for the time I did not work` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I still paid for the time I did not work` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I still paid for the time I did not work` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ss 78A, 78B, 78E(3). Inputs: treatment, reason, substantial, reasonable, to comply.
#ASSERT `Has my employer discriminated against me under s 78A` `dismissed me` `I raised a health or safety issue or concern` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has my employer discriminated against me under s 78A` `dismissed me` `I raised a health or safety issue or concern` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has my employer discriminated against me under s 78A` `dismissed me` `another reason` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has my employer discriminated against me under s 78A` `none of these` `I raised a health or safety issue or concern` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 78E(3): both limbs proved: a defence.
#ASSERT `Has my employer discriminated against me under s 78A` `dismissed me` `I raised a health or safety issue or concern` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Only limb (a) proved: no defence.
#ASSERT `Has my employer discriminated against me under s 78A` `dismissed me` `I raised a health or safety issue or concern` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A prospective employee refused a job for having been a health and safety representative.
#ASSERT `Has my employer discriminated against me under s 78A` `refused or failed to offer me employment` `I am or was a health and safety representative or committee member` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has my employer discriminated against me under s 78A` `altered my position to my detriment` `I assisted or gave information to an inspector, the Authority, a union authorised representative, a representative or a committee member` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 76. Inputs: treatment, reason, dominant.
#ASSERT `Could my employer be guilty under s 76` `dismissed me` `I assisted or gave information to an inspector, the Authority, a union authorised representative, a representative or a committee member` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Could my employer be guilty under s 76` `dismissed me` `I assisted or gave information to an inspector, the Authority, a union authorised representative, a representative or a committee member` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Could my employer be guilty under s 76` `dismissed me` `another reason` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Could my employer be guilty under s 76` `threatened to do one of those things` `I exercised a power as a representative or committee member` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 78E(1): not more than 1 year after the day the plaintiff knew or ought to have known.
#ASSERT (`By when must I start my discrimination claim` (`d` 15 3 2026)) `is the same day as` (`d` 15 3 2027)
#ASSERT (`By when must I start my discrimination claim` (`d` 31 1 2026)) `is the same day as` (`d` 31 1 2027)
-- 29 February 2028 + 12 months: there is no 29 February 2029, so 28 February 2029.
#ASSERT (`By when must I start my discrimination claim` (`d` 29 2 2028)) `is the same day as` (`d` 28 2 2029)
#ASSERT `Is my discrimination claim in time` (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2027)
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is my discrimination claim in time` (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 16 3 2027)))

-- s 78D(5), 78E(5)-(6). Inputs: eligible, contravened, s 78 order already made.
#ASSERT `Can the court make a s 78D order for me` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the court make a s 78D order for me` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the court make a s 78D order for me` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the court make a s 78D order for me` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ss 77, 78E(2).
#ASSERT `Must my employer prove its reason` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my employer prove its reason` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 131(1): 10 January 2026 + 6 months = 10 July 2026; a request may be made from 11 July 2026.
#ASSERT `May I ask WorkSafe to prosecute` (`d` 10 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 10 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I ask WorkSafe to prosecute` (`d` 10 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 11 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I ask WorkSafe to prosecute` (`d` 10 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 11 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 31 August 2025 + 6 months = 28 February 2026 (no 31 February); a request from 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `May I ask WorkSafe to prosecute` (`d` 31 8 2025) FALSE (`d` 28 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I ask WorkSafe to prosecute` (`d` 31 8 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 131(2), (2A): within 3 months after receipt.
#ASSERT (`By when must WorkSafe answer my request` (`d` 5 2 2026)) `is the same day as` (`d` 5 5 2026)
#ASSERT (`By when must WorkSafe answer my request` (`d` 30 11 2025)) `is the same day as` (`d` 28 2 2026)
#ASSERT (`By when must WorkSafe answer my request` (`d` 31 5 2026)) `is the same day as` (`d` 31 8 2026)
-- 5 February to 5 May 2026 is 23 + 31 + 30 + 5 = 89 days. An answer on day 89 is in time; on day 90 it is late.
#ASSERT `Has WorkSafe answered in time` (`d` 5 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 5 5 2026) (`d` 5 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has WorkSafe answered in time` (`d` 5 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 6 5 2026) (`d` 6 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has WorkSafe answered in time` (`d` 5 2 2026) TRUE (`d` 20 2 2026) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has WorkSafe answered in time` (`d` 5 2 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 5 5 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Has WorkSafe answered in time` (`d` 5 2 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 6 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 131(3): 5 February 2026 + 9 months = 5 November 2026; with no prosecution, from 6 November 2026.
#ASSERT `May I ask for a referral to the DPP` (`d` 5 2 2026) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I ask for a referral to the DPP` (`d` 5 2 2026) FALSE FALSE (`d` 5 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I ask for a referral to the DPP` (`d` 5 2 2026) FALSE FALSE (`d` 6 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I ask for a referral to the DPP` (`d` 5 2 2026) FALSE TRUE (`d` 6 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 132. Inputs: offence, officer manslaughter charge, notice day, coroner, coroner day, undertaking, undertaking day,
-- DPP authorisation, fresh evidence, day of prosecution.
-- (a) Notice 1 March 2024 + 2 years = 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `Can it still be prosecuted` `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can it still be prosecuted` `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 2 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) An inquest ended 1 June 2025 + 1 year = 1 June 2026, the latest.
#ASSERT `Can it still be prosecuted` `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can it still be prosecuted` `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 2 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) An undertaking contravened 1 May 2026 + 6 months = 1 November 2026.
#ASSERT `Can it still be prosecuted` `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 1 5 2026) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can it still be prosecuted` `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 1 5 2026) FALSE FALSE (`d` 2 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (d) the DPP's written authorisation, and s 132(2) fresh evidence.
#ASSERT `Can it still be prosecuted` `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can it still be prosecuted` `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 132(3): workplace manslaughter at any time, including an officer's s 144(1) offence for a s 39G(1) contravention.
#ASSERT `Can it still be prosecuted` `s 39G(1) workplace manslaughter` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2021) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2040) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can it still be prosecuted` `s 39G(2) workplace manslaughter by an officer` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2021) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2040) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can it still be prosecuted` `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2021) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2040) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A summary offence: s 132 does not speak.
#ASSERT `Can it still be prosecuted` `s 35 duty to consult` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT (`What is the last day to prosecute` `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000)) `is just the day` (`d` 1 3 2026)
#ASSERT (`What is the last day to prosecute` `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000)) `is just the day` (`d` 1 6 2026)
-- An inquest ended 1 January 2025 + 1 year = 1 January 2026, earlier than (a): (a) stands.
#ASSERT (`What is the last day to prosecute` `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000)) `is just the day` (`d` 1 3 2026)
-- An undertaking withdrawn 31 August 2026 + 6 months = 28 February 2027.
#ASSERT (`What is the last day to prosecute` `s 23(1) employer's duty to other persons` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 31 8 2026)) `is just the day` (`d` 28 2 2027)
#ASSERT `is no day` (`What is the last day to prosecute` `s 39G(2) workplace manslaughter by an officer` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000))
#ASSERT `is no day` (`What is the last day to prosecute` `s 21(1) employer's duty to employees` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000))
#ASSERT `is no day` (`What is the last day to prosecute` `s 22(1) employer's duty to monitor and inform` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000))

-- The s 131(2) rule itself (clock: days from receipt; 89 days for a request received 5 February 2026).
#TRACE `s 131(2) -- the Authority must report to the person who asked within 3 months` 89 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Authority` DOES `report in writing to the person who made the request` AT 89
-- expect: FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 131(2) -- the Authority must report to the person who asked within 3 months` 89 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person who asked` DOES `wait` AT 90
-- expect: BREACH BY `the Authority`
